[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137529,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pilomatricoma is a benign cutaneous adnexal neoplasm that shows differentiation towards matrical cells and the hair cortex.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137530,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8110/0 Pilomatricoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137531,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F22 &amp; XH9E37 Benign neoplasms of epidermal appendages &amp; Pilomatricoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137532,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> pilomatrixoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> calcifying epithelioma of Malherbe.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137533,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137534,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pilomatricoma mostly involves the upper eyelids and medial eyebrow area {10355837;24801260;18929763;9704827;21769234;13700704}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137535,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pilomatricoma usually presents as a solitary, well-defined, painless, slowly growing, subcutaneous reddish-blue mass, which is firm and freely mobile, and has a gritty sensation due to calcification {7494166;18929763}. It can show rapid growth due to inflammation {18929763;31358136}. It is usually &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm in diameter. Calcification may result in the tent sign due to angulation of the tumour {14663221;24838222}. Multiple lesions have been described {9704827;14663221;24838222}.</p>\r\n<p>High-resolution MRI allows the identification of most eyelid structures and can assess the precise location of pilomatricomas inside the eyelid {32178233}. Furthermore, MRI aids in the differential diagnosis of eyelid masses, and perfusion-weighted imaging helps in differentiating a pilomatricoma from a malignant eyelid mass. Although it is a benign lesion, a low apparent diffusion coefficient can be seen, probably due to the presence of calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137536,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The M:F&nbsp;ratio in White people is 2:3 {18929763}. It has a bimodal presentation, with one peak in children and young adults (40% in the first decade of life and 20% in the second decade of life) and another peak between 50&nbsp;and 65&nbsp;years of age {18929763;9704827;11829174}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137537,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most are sporadic. Familial and multiple cases are linked to genetic conditions such as myotonic muscular dystrophy, Gardner syndrome, basal cell naevus syndrome, and xeroderma pigmentosum {14663221;5039107}. Associations with blunt trauma, hypercalcaemia, and sarcoidosis {29763996;18929763} are reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137538,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pathogenesis has been linked to disruption of the hair growth anagen phase {18929763} and to the <em>CTNNB1</em> gene mutation {11472567}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137539,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions appear as pink to tan-coloured well-circumscribed firm nodules that may be pseudoencapsulated {32304502;31358136}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137540,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour comprises one or several dermal nodules. The periphery of the nodules shows mitotically active basaloid cells, with scant cytoplasm. An intermediate zone shows smaller pyknotic basophilic nuclei with a paler cytoplasm and the central area shows shadow cells with eosinophilic cytoplasm and non-staining empty nuclei centrally {28457306;32304502}. Shadow cells may calcify over time {18929763}. Focal granulomatous inflammation, sheets of keratin-like material, and foreign body&ndash;type giant cells are also common {18929763;14048805;34119944}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137541,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNAB produces smears with recognizable clusters of basaloid cells and foreign body&ndash;type multinucleated cells {29370510;30498290}. Ghost cells can be difficult to find {29370510}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137542,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137543,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> the presence of basaloid cells at the periphery, an intermediate zone with smaller pyknotic basophilic nuclei, and eosinophilic shadow (ghost) cells centrally.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137544,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137545,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrence has been reported in 1.4% of cases in one series within an average time of 1.6&nbsp;years {14663221}. Malignant transformation into pilomatrix carcinoma is rare {7995429}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]